Every route-marker producer hand-rolls its Symbol record, and they drifted
apart in the four ways the validators check: an id kind-slot left as the
literal `route` fossil (`route` is not a registered symbol kind ->
id_format), an absent origin_run_id (cross_field), an unregistered origin
pass-id (axis_conformance), and -- newly measured here -- an id NAME-slot
that does not round-trip against Symbol.name (ADR-0036 Ruling 1).

`analyze.base.make_route_symbol` encapsulates the shape that
framework_patterns.materialize_route_symbols already proved for the
go/js/java trio, so a producer is fixed by routing through it rather than
by re-deriving the invariant.

Naming is FORCED, not stylistic: Symbol.name is "{METHOD} {path}" with the
handler in meta.handler_ref (what linkers/route_handler already resolves
against). A multi-method registration -- Starlette methods=['GET','POST'],
a Django CBV expanded per verb -- emits several markers at the SAME span,
so only the method+path pair keeps their ids distinct; a handler-derived
name-slot would collide them. Pinned by a regression test.

GATE BEFORE SWEEP. test_route_marker_id_name_slot_round_trips asserts the
round-trip per language; not-yet-migrated producers sit in NAME_SLOT_HOLES
as a STRICT xfail so a migration XPASSes and forces promotion (the
ROUTE_HOLES idiom). Deliberately a marker, not an imperative
pytest.xfail() -- the imperative form always reports xfail and can never
XPASS, which would record the hole while silently disabling the ratchet
meant to close it.

Measured baseline over the route-parity corpus:
  java, javascript  -- clean (already mint via the materializer)
  python, rust      -- 0 markers (routes surface as concept=route; their
                       direct producers need their own fixtures)
  go                -- LIVE VIOLATION: mints inline with name=handler_name
                       against an id name-slot of "{METHOD} {path}" -- the
                       same inverted Pattern B WI-vuzaf filed as
                       Starlette-specific, inside the cohort WI-tufil had
                       declared clean.

No producer is migrated in this commit; the fleet (go, py.py Django/
Starlette/Flask-RESTful, ruby, php, elixir, swift, play_routes, js_ts,
grpc, annotation_convention) stays tracked on WI-zugob, which describes
itself as batchable one-producer-per-PR.

